[[460.0,-0.2378],[465.0,-0.1534],[470.0,0.0609],[475.0,0.2346],[480.0,0.3835],[485.0,0.5123],[490.0,0.6242],[495.0,0.7207],[500.0,0.7985],[505.0,0.8629],[510.0,0.9161],[515.0,0.9645],[520.0,1.0151],[525.0,1.096],[530.0,1.1891],[535.0,1.2767],[540.0,1.3549],[545.0,1.4205],[550.0,1.472],[555.0,1.4992],[560.0,1.4992],[565.0,1.4669],[570.0,1.3796],[575.0,1.1635],[580.0,0.8651],[585.0,0.5508],[590.0,0.2305],[595.0,-0.0799],[600.0,-0.2]],"r":[[560.0,0.0268],[565.0,0.0308],[570.0,0.2622],[575.0,0.4962],[580.0,0.685],[585.0,0.8537],[590.0,0.9663],[595.0,1.054],[600.0,1.1262],[605.0,1.1804],[610.0,1.2164],[615.0,1.2378],[620.0,1.252],[625.0,1.2614],[630.0,1.2692],[635.0,1.2756],[640.0,1.2772],[645.0,1.2732],[650.0,1.2326],[655.0,1.1127],[660.0,0.8737],[665.0,0.5721],[670.0,0.2407],[675.0,-0.0398],[680.0,-0.085]]},"source":{"document":"AF3-0217E","date":"2006-10","file":"fuji-superia-xtra-400.pdf","url":"https://asset.fujifilm.com/www/uk/files/2019-09/af234c58ab3d3b67b41cde22b1155309/films_superia-xtra400_datasheet_01.pdf","sha256":"7e77f9c3bd3001e40f8cafea55c73cdfda09fd1980b55b73862d6da87f6a11b2"},"notes":["Fujicolor Superia X-TRA 400 [CH], Fujifilm Product Information Bulletin, plots on page 6 (nos. 17, 18 and 20). Process printed on the plots: CN-16 (the bulletin also allows CN-16Q/FA/L/S and Process C-41). Date taken from the print code KAMIQ-06.10-FP next to the reference number in the footer (no other date printed).","Speed: daylight ISO 400/27 degrees; 3200 K tungsten ISO 100/21 degrees with Wratten 80A (Fuji LBB-12). No Log H Ref is printed (log_h_ref null); the bulletin says an 18% grey card read through the Red Status M filter should give density 0.75-0.95.","curves: x is log H in lux-seconds as printed (daylight, 1/125 s); all three curves are solid and never touch, traced end to end on the vector paths (D-min plateaus about 0.73 b, 0.46 g, 0.14 r). The last point of each line can lie up to one 0.05 step beyond the drawn end (the tool extends its grid by flat extrapolation).","sensitivity: the y axis has NO numbers, only a double arrow marking 1.0 between two horizontal rules. y is therefore set to 1.0 on the upper rule and 0.0 on the lower rule: the zero is arbitrary, only differences between points and between layers are meaningful. Sensitivity = reciprocal of the exposure in J/cm2 giving density 1.0 above D-min (Status M, CN-16).","sensitivity: each layer ends in a near-vertical drop (blue ends about 510 nm, green starts about 460 nm and ends about 600 nm, red starts about 565 nm and ends about 680 nm); the tool keeps one y per x, so the last few nm of the drops are approximated, and the first/last sample on the 5 nm grid can be a flat extension of up to 5 nm.","dyes: the plot is not of separate cyan/magenta/yellow dyes but of two curves, Mid-scale Density (mid; typical densities for a mid-scale neutral subject) and Minimum Density (min; D-min), 400-720 nm, y = spectral diffuse density as printed (0-2.5).","Grain: diffuse RMS granularity value 4 (micro-densitometer aperture 48 um diameter, sample density 1.0 above minimum density; Fujifilm measurement, not comparable with colour reversal film)."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier","grain":{"grain":16.0,"grain_size":32.0,"grain_roughness":50.0}}